    {usesProfile && <p class="small" style="margin-top:6px"><b><L t="Profile step." p="Share of the stars inside the ring." /></b> <L t={`This lens’s stellar mass inside R_E comes from the profile step (a printed total × the light-profile fraction). The same step, run on the SLACS totals, gives ${ps.map((g) => `${g.key}: median ${g.stats.median.toFixed(3)}, range ${g.stats.min.toFixed(3)}–${g.stats.max.toFixed(3)}, ${g.stats.within} of ${g.stats.n} within ±10%`).join('; ')} of R13’s printed masses inside R_E (D-075 item 5). Reported, not pass/fail.`} p="The way the star mass inside the ring is worked out here was tested on another survey that prints both numbers; the results are on the dataset page." /> <a href={`${dsPage}#check-profile`}><L t="The check in full" p="See the check" /></a></p>}
